major announcement from Amazon Amazon  has announced that it is going to be  opening a grocery store in Seattle  Washington early in 2017 what is notable  about this grocery store well it's not  going to have any cashiers in fact it's  going to need very very few employees  because the way it's going to work is  when you walk in you will scan your  phone which will tell the store that  you're inside and then they will have a  very sophisticated system that uses  sensors computer vision deep learning  which will track customers as they move  through the store and it will register  what items you pick up and put in your  basket you'd change your mind and put an  item back on the shelves the system will  be able to determine that as well  there's going to be prepared food salad  sandwiches etcetera that will all be  handmade but it will be sold in boxes  that are also part of the entire  automated system and then when you're  done you just walk out of the store  because the system tracks what you have  in your basket there's no need to check  out it'll just automatically be billed  to your credit card on file  so obviously Amazon is talking about  this as total utopia uh it's gonna cut  down on lines it's going to cut down on  a lot of the stuff that's annoying about  going grocery shopping particularly in  urban areas but there's the other side  of this which is this would be a major  job killer if you think about the 3.4  million people who were employed as  cashiers in the United States according  to the US Labor Bureau of Labor  Statistics and if you think about the  4.5 million employed as retail  salespeople and the 2.4 million  employees laborers that are stocking  shelves and moving cargo around Amazon  is automating away many of these jobs  they already have robots in warehouses  to move cargo around they have new  robots that are able to not only find  items on shelves but also prepare items  for shipment this is something that I  truly believe pat is inevitable when we  look at the advance of Technology and  you go to a grocery store and you see a  cashier scanning items one by one and  punching in produce uh stock codes  that does not strike me as something  that is remotely necessary five or ten  years down the line given all of the  technological developments that we have  why are we going to need cashiers to  scan your items in many stores already  putting in in place itself uh self  checkouts uh but I I don't believe that  pushing back against this because it's  going to be a job killer is going to be  effective because when you just look at  what the job is and what technology can  do how do you justify millions of  cashiers just ringing products through a  scanner right it seems like cashiers  will be the next victim of automation  and technology but it's overall a good  thing I mean scribes were upset hundreds  of years ago in the printing press came  out I have a friend who won't use self  checkouts because he doesn't want to  encourage stores to put in self  checkouts it's a very nice gesture but  it is going to do nothing to stop this  and the broader analysis here is we had  a very drawn-out presidential election  campaign with tons of discussion about  bringing jobs back and manufacturing  jobs etcetera etcetera no serious  discussion of the fact that many of the  jobs Trump wants to bring back no longer  exists and the more important discussion  that jobs are going to be destroyed by  technology up I don't believe that  pushing back about against this is going  to be effective whether it's Amazon or  someone else if you really just think  about where technology is right now and  then you think about lots of the jobs  that still exist it's very hard to  justify those jobs still existing 510 or  at the most fifteen years down the line
 

